===Etymology===
Confer A. S. {{term|hereberga}} or {{term|herebeorga}}; Old English {{term|herberowe}}, {{term|harbrough}} and {{term|herber}}. Modern English {{term|harbour}} and {{term|arbour}}; middle High German {{term|herberge}}; German {{term|herberge}}; Swedish {{term|herberge}}; hence Italian {{term|albergo}} and French {{term|auberge}}.

===Noun===
'''herbergi''' {{n}}
# a [[harbour]]
# an [[inn]]
# a [[closet]],a [[room]]

==== Derived terms ====
